-- #1111 A-2.5 (#1092) MIRROR CELL — the same defect with both halves flipped, so
-- a fix that merely swapped which interface wins the bare-name race cannot pass
-- both this and `1092_method_scope_named_b`.
--
-- `mth` is selected from `msa` ONLY, so the occurrence means `MA.mth`.  `Blob`
-- implements `MB` and has no `MA` impl, so `check` must report exactly one error:
--
--   No impl of MA for Blob; write an 'impl MA Blob'.
--
-- 🚨 BEFORE THE FIX this checked clean, exit 0, and printed `2` — `MB`'s impl body
-- for a call spelled `MA.mth`.  Note the import lines are in the SAME textual
-- order as the flagship's, and only which module's `mth` is selected changes:
-- under the old bare-name table the checked-against interface depended ONLY on
-- module load order, so both files' verdicts moved together; under the use-site
-- rule they move independently, which is what these two fixtures pin.
import msa.{MA, mth}
import msb.{MB}

public export data Blob = Blob

export impl MB Blob where
  mth b = 2

main = println (mth Blob)
